    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0061","sequence":73,
      "meaning":"Kinnaras, nāgas, siddhas, gandharvas and all the gods depart with their wives; except for Viṣṇu, Brahmā and Maheśa, every god sets out in splendid array. Satī sees many kinds of beautiful celestial vehicles crossing the sky. Divine women sing melodies whose sound could break sages’ meditation. When she asks, Śiva explains that her father is holding a sacrifice, and she feels some joy. She thinks that, if Maheśa permits, she might use this occasion to stay there a few days. Though her husband’s withdrawal pains her, she does not speak of it, mindful of her own offense. With fear, hesitation and love mingled in her charming words, she asks the compassionate Lord’s leave to go respectfully witness the great celebration at her father’s house.",
