    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0062","sequence":74,
      "meaning":"Śiva says her wish is good and pleases him, but Dakṣa has improperly sent no invitation. Dakṣa called all his daughters yet, from hostility toward Śiva, forgot Satī too; resentment from Brahmā’s assembly still makes him insulting. If she goes uninvited, courtesy, affection and honor will not remain. One may visit the homes of a friend, master, father or teacher without invitation, but no welfare follows where hostility is acknowledged. Śambhu reasons with her in many ways, yet under destiny’s power wisdom does not enter her heart. He says that going uninvited does not seem good to him. After every effort fails to detain Dakṣa’s daughter, Tripurāri sends his chief attendants with her and bids her farewell.",
