    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0063","sequence":75,
      "meaning":"When Bhavānī reaches her father’s house, fear of Dakṣa prevents anyone from honoring her. Only her mother receives her respectfully; her sisters greet her with much smiling. Dakṣa neither asks after her welfare nor hides the burning of his whole body at seeing her. At the sacrifice Satī sees no share assigned to Śambhu. Śaṅkara’s warning returns to mind, and recognition of her Lord’s humiliation burns her heart. Her earlier pain had not pierced her like this great torment. Though the world contains many terrible sorrows, dishonor from one’s own kin is hardest. Understanding this, Satī grows intensely angry despite her mother’s many attempts to counsel her. Unable to endure Śiva’s insult or calm her heart, she forcefully silences the whole assembly and speaks in wrath.",
