    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0064","sequence":76,
      "meaning":"Satī addresses the assembly and eminent sages: all who uttered or heard Śaṅkara’s slander will immediately reap its fruit, and her father too will repent fully. She states the rule for hearing abuse of a saint, Śambhu or Śrīpati: one able to do so should cut out the slanderer’s tongue; otherwise one should cover one’s ears and depart. Maheśa, Tripura’s foe, is the world’s very Self, father and benefactor. Since her foolish father reviles him and this body arose from Dakṣa’s seed, she will abandon it at once, holding moon-crested Vṛṣaketu in her heart. Saying this, she burns her body in yogic fire and the entire sacrifice erupts in lamentation. Hearing of Satī’s death, Śambhu’s attendants begin wrecking the rite; seeing the sacrifice’s destruction, the great sage Bhṛgu mounts a defense.",
