    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0065","sequence":77,
      "meaning":"Śaṅkara receives the full news and wrathfully sends Vīrabhadra. Vīrabhadra goes, destroys the sacrifice and gives every god the due fruit of his conduct. Dakṣa’s fate becomes known throughout the world—the natural result of turning against Śambhu. Since everyone knows this account, the poet tells it briefly. As Satī dies she asks Hari for the boon of love for Śiva’s feet birth after birth. Therefore she goes to Himālaya’s house and is born in Pārvatī’s body. From Umā’s arrival, every accomplishment and prosperity spreads there. Sages establish beautiful hermitages everywhere, and the snow mountain provides suitable dwellings. All trees bear flowers and fruit continually, fresh varieties flourish, and many kinds of jewel mines appear upon the lovely mountain.",
